course: dictionary
lesson: 10598
title: Undertake and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undertake is a formal verb, so you will meet it in books, news and exams. It can mean to take on a job or task and be responsible for it. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «The council will undertake a survey of the park.» Here undertake means they will start the survey and take charge of it. Ask yourself: does «start and take charge of» fit in the sentence instead of the hard word?
explain: Writers sometimes give you a clue in brackets. The Badger writes, «Toad has at last seen the error of his ways … he has undertaken (promised) to give up motor-cars entirely and for ever.» The brackets tell you undertaken means promised.
fact: Undertake means to take on a job or task, often a big or hard one.
fact: Undertake can also mean to promise to do something, as in «He undertook to pay the money back.»
fact: Undertaking, as a noun, means a big task or a promise.
fact: In UK driving talk, undertake means to overtake a car on the wrong side, the inside lane, which is dangerous.
fact: The forms change: undertook is the past tense, and undertaken is used after has or have, as in «He has undertaken to help».
exercise: «She will undertake the difficult task of painting the school hall.» What does undertake mean here? | Lose on purpose | *Take on and do | Look at quickly | Give up and go home
exercise: The Badger writes, «Toad has undertaken (promised) to give up motor-cars.» What does the bracket tell you undertaken means? | Broken | *Promised | Bought | Forgotten
exercise: Dad says, «Never undertake on a motorway.» What does undertake mean in driving talk? | Turn around safely | *Pass another car on the wrong side, the inside lane | Honk at a friend | Stop at a red light
test: «The scientists will undertake an investigation into the river.» What does undertake mean? | Measure the depth only | Swim across the river | Stop and forget about | *Start and take responsibility for
test: «It was a huge undertaking, and the team was proud to finish it.» What does undertaking mean here? | A wet day | A quiet rest | A small game | *A big task or promise
exam: The Badger says Toad «undertook» to give up cars. What does undertook mean? | *Promised | Ignored | Broke | Sold
